      "type": "ORDER_ROULETTE",
      "transition": "slide",
      "background": "zoneA",
      "narration": "Here's the catch though. If one test assumes another ran first, workers grab them in any order at all. So it passes. Then fails. Then fails differently. Then passes again. That's not a broken test, that's a coin flip — and a broken test at least stays broken while you fix it.",
